      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,600 mg/day of ibuprofen is three times the maximum daily dose, and I know of no indication that supports it. At that dose the risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and metabolic and CNS toxicity is high, and it wouldn't give more benefit. Analgesic and anti-inflammatory effects plateau well below it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** Examples are 600 mg PO four times daily, 800 mg PO three times daily, or 400 mg PO every 6 hours.\n- **Help you with a different problem.** If the pain or inflammation isn't controlled at the maximum dose, you could add acetaminophen or consider another agent. Pharmacy can help with that.\n- **Go through pharmacy or your attending.** If you think there's an unusual reason for this dose, they can review it and enter it through the proper channels.\n\nTell me which option you want, and I'll enter the order right away."
      }
